     "type": "application",
     "title": "Install Time Blocking This Week",
     "content": "Install time blocking for your ONE Thing this week. Step one: open your calendar and block time off first, scheduling at least one genuine rest period you will honor. Step two: block your ONE Thing by reserving a large chunk of your highest-energy hours, aiming for up to four unbroken hours in the morning if possible, and enter it as a recurring, non-negotiable appointment rather than a vague intention. Step three: block a short weekly planning session to review your goals and choose next week's priorities. Step four: protect your ONE Thing block using Keller's four tactics. Build a bunker by choosing a specific distraction-free location. Store provisions by gathering everything you will need in advance so you never leave mid-session. Sweep for mines by silencing your phone, closing email, and blocking distracting sites before you begin. Enlist support by telling the key people in your life about your block and asking them to respect it. Step five: at the end of the week, count how many of your blocks you completed intact and identify what interrupted the ones you lost, then strengthen that specific defense next week. Treat every attempt to steal your block as a test of your commitment to your ONE Thing. Keller's promise is direct: people who time block their priority and defend it relentlessly accomplish more than those who work far longer with open, unprotected calendars. Your calendar is a statement of what you value. Block your ONE Thing first, protect it like a fortress, and watch your most important work finally get done.",
